highlight.js, vendored.

  version:  11.11.1
  source:   https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/highlight.js/11.11.1/highlight.min.js
  sha256:   see `shasum -a 256 highlight.min.js`
  license:  BSD-3-Clause, in highlight.min.js.LICENSE
  bundle:   the "common" build -- 36 languages, listed by hljs.listLanguages()

It is vendored rather than loaded from a CDN because the review page is served
from an ephemeral loopback port inside Medusa's own binary: a page that has to
reach the internet to colour a diff would be blank on a plane, and asking the
network for the code that renders a local file is not a dependency this tool
should have. It is embedded, so it ships in the binary and needs no build step.

To upgrade: replace both files from the same version tag, run the review page,
and check that a Go, a Python and a YAML file still highlight. `languageFor` in
review.html maps file extensions onto hljs language ids, so a bundle with fewer
languages silently degrades those files to plain text rather than breaking.
